    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d765">

                <pb facs="0799" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/420a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-28T19:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1939—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>211. Department is advised that groups representing Spanish Loyalist Government
                    are endeavoring to arrange for ships to evacuate Spanish refugees principally
                    from Valencia and Alicante. They fear such ships might be taken by the warships
                    under control of General Franco unless assistance were given them by French and
                    British Navy patrols so as to insure that they would not be captured or sunk.
                    Kindly inquire of the Foreign Office whether the government contemplates
                    assisting ships bearing refugees to escape.</p>
                <p>This also sent to London.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d765-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
